  "notes": "Original procedural construction. Cosmetic glass debris: flat angular fragments fractured from thin plates, ONE OBJECT PER SHARD so a game can fling each piece separately -- the art leg of the replicated-destructible pattern, where shards are local cosmetics and never networked state. Scattered footprint reads as fallen glass under a broken pane. Collisionless by construction, like the other dressing debris: a sliver of glass must never block a route or a beam. TRANSPARENCY: rides the glass kind's Pixelcoat pack hint; the flat fallback is opaque vertex color, matching the window pane's own fallback."
